From f42ba8a84b815d636667af6df733b97fd2664250 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tb <tb@local>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 14:59:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 27/27] tb710fu: Type-C DP orientation fixes and bring-up log
 diet

qmp-combo:
- Never rebuild the COM block on an orientation change.  Record the new
  orientation and let the next com_init() (0->1 refcount) program
  TYPEC_CTRL/PHY_MODE_CTRL from it.  Rebuilding underneath a live DP link
  left the DP PHY held in reset because qmpphy_mode was USB3_ONLY.
- Split the mode/orientation programming out of com_init() into
  qmp_combo_com_set_mode() so the "keep COM for USB3" fast path can rewrite
  the mode bits without a full com_exit/com_init.
- In that fast path stop the USB3 PCS before rewriting TYPEC_CTRL; writing
  it while the SuperSpeed port is polling hangs the bus.
- Guard dp_exit() against a negative init_count on an unbalanced
  phy_exit() (otherwise the next com_init() silently skips programming).

pmic_glink_altmode:
- Acknowledge notifications for ports that have no connector node; a left
  unacknowledged notification stops the firmware from reporting further
  connections (UCSI port latch).
- Delay only the DP connect HPD report by tb_hpd_delay_ms (default 1000,
  0 = off).  The connector used to be reported connected while the dock's
  SuperSpeed/USB2 hubs were still enumerating; KWin then enabled the output
  in that window and a DPU register write on the settling PHY reset the SoC.
  Unplug, the ACK and the mux switch all stay immediate; the delayed work
  re-checks hpd_state/svid/mux_ctrl before reporting.

Log diet (these investigations are closed):
- ucsi_glink, wcd939x-usbss: dev_info/pr_info -> dev_dbg/pr_debug.
- qmp-combo: keep-COM and USB3-init-wait messages -> debug.
- altmode: per-notification port dump -> dev_dbg (keep the one-line
  "deferred DP connect report").
- nt36xxx: 11-line point-data checksum hex dump -> pr_debug (the one-line
  "checksum not match" stays); missing "usb" power supply -> debug.
- dsi_host: DSI underflow register dump and status line -> debug.
- aw882xx: DEBUG stays on so aw_dev_err() remains pr_err(); aw_dev_info()
  is compiled out unless TB710FU_AW_VERBOSE is set.

Verified on the TB710FU: 8 plug/flip cycles with DP streaming, no reset and
exactly one connector probe per plug; idle kernel log growth is 0 lines/min.
